## Exact next work and unchanged boundary

The next successor must implement the exact SCM_RIGHTS bootstrap transport and
dedicated broker child, connect the adopted listener to the frozen scalar broker
loop, and prove the sealed READY/release channel's origin, peer exclusivity,
one-byte consumption and lifecycle order. The parent must obtain and own
aggregate receipt/reap evidence while every receive, ID-validation, response or
transport failure remains inside the guardian's retirement boundary.

After that comes integration into the frozen bootstrap/dispatcher/lifecycle,
successor source-closure authentication, and a separately authorized bounded
Linux native qualification. Only a passing native qualification can return to
the unchanged host, input, resource and real-import admission gates. These are
remaining parts of Gate 5, not new roadmap gates.

GPU is not needed for the next local integration work. The S3-backed pretrained
checkpoint remains the intended base, but no current remote availability check
was made. Real import, training and production remain disabled.
